## 2. GGUF Split: Reject Non-Contiguous Shard Numbers

**Component:** `include/strata/artifact/gguf_split.hpp` — `gguf_split_paths()`

**Responsibilities:** Resolves any shard path to the full ordered list of shard paths for a split model, verifying each file exists.

**Problem:** The function rewrites only the five-digit shard number and checks existence, but does not verify that the parsed `no` matches the position in the returned list. A file named `model-00003-of-00005.gguf` passed as `any` produces paths for shards 1–5, but if shard 3 was renamed to shard 4 and the original shard 4 deleted, the existence check passes for the wrong file. More critically, if a user passes a path whose `no` field is inconsistent with the filename pattern (e.g., a symlink with a mismatched name), the function silently returns a list that does not include the passed file.

**Proposed change:**

```diff
--- a/include/strata/artifact/gguf_split.hpp
+++ b/include/strata/artifact/gguf_split.hpp
@@ -38,6 +38,12 @@
     if (n < 1 || no < 1 || no > n) return {any};
     std::vector<std::string> out;
     for (int i = 1; i <= n; ++i) {
         char num[8];
         std::snprintf(num, sizeof num, "%05d", i);
         std::string p = any;
         p.replace(at - 5, 5, num);
+        // The passed path must appear in the resolved list; a symlink or renamed file whose
+        // name disagrees with its content's split.no would otherwise produce a list that
+        // silently omits the file the caller opened.
+        if (i == no && p != any)
+            throw std::runtime_error("gguf_split_paths: the passed path '" + any +
+                "' does not match the shard number it declares (expected shard " +
+                std::to_string(no) + " to be '" + p + "')");
         if (!std::ifstream(p, std::ios::binary))
             throw std::runtime_error("missing model shard " + p + " (shard " + std::to_string(i) + " of " +
                                      std::to_string(n) + "; is the download complete?)");
         out.push_back(std::move(p));
     }
     return out;
```

**Verification cases:**
1. **Mismatched symlink:** Create a directory with `model-00001-of-00002.gguf` and `model-00002-of-00002.gguf`. Create a symlink `model-00001-of-00002.gguf` → `model-00002-of-00002.gguf` (so the name says shard 1 but the content is shard 2). Passing the symlink path must throw with the mismatch message.
2. **Normal 4-shard model:** Pass any of the four Unsloth UD-Q4_K_XL shard paths. The function must return all four paths in order without throwing.

